release.body:
# Project Titan Magenta Edition — BIG UPDATE

This release is one of the largest revisions of Project Titan Magenta Edition so far.

The **BIG UPDATE** brings a new round of system-level improvements focused on networking, game execution, stability, usability and the native Titan environment.

> **Project Titan is not just a launcher.**
> It is a PlayStation 2 operating-system project and native application platform with its own boot chain, runtime services, scheduling, package infrastructure, system APIs and integrated game backends.

## Highlights

### Cheats & Graphics Enhancements

Project Titan now includes integrated per-game patch support for both **Titan Neutrino** and **Titan UL**.

Games can now expose dedicated:

- **Cheats**
- **Graphics Enhancements**

menus directly from the Titan interface.

The system supports persistent selections, automatic enhancement presets, experimental patches and safe per-title patch databases.

When graphical enhancements are active, Titan can identify the game as **Titan Enhanced** during launch.

Gameplay cheats are kept separate from visual enhancements, with dedicated handling and a few very Titan-like messages when you decide to make the game a little easier. :)

### Network improvements

This revision contains another significant pass over Titan's network subsystem, including improvements to:

- network initialization;
- service stability;
- connection handling;
- background network activity;
- resource ownership and cleanup;
- integration with Titan system services.

The goal is not only to make networking more reliable, but to continue treating it as a real operating-system service rather than functionality owned by individual applications.

### Stability improvements

A large amount of work in this revision happened below the visible interface.

The BIG UPDATE includes fixes and hardening across:

- runtime lifecycle management;
- memory and resource ownership;
- game handoff paths;
- background services;
- storage operations;
- native application execution;
- boot/runtime coordination;
- failure recovery;
- system cleanup between workloads.

Several regressions discovered through real-world testing were also addressed during this development cycle.

### Native application platform improvements

Project Titan continues evolving beyond game launching.

The system provides its own environment for native Titan applications, including:

- Titan runtime APIs;
- package installation infrastructure;
- TPKG applications;
- scheduling and lifecycle services;
- shared input, audio, graphics and storage services;
- system notifications;
- networking APIs;
- memory/VRAM management strategies;
- Titan-specific optimization systems for native software.

Game launching remains an important part of Project Titan, but it is only one subsystem of the larger platform.

## Game execution

The update preserves the established production game backends:

- **Titan Neutrino**
- **Titan UL**

while adding the new game-patch infrastructure around them without replacing the validated production engine binaries.

Project Titan now has a cleaner separation between:

- game execution;
- gameplay cheats;
- graphical enhancements;
- system runtime services.

## Release packages

Two packages are provided.

### `TITAN_SYSTEM.TINS`

The packaged Project Titan system image intended for supported Titan installation/update workflows.

### Installerless package

A manual installation package for users who want to deploy the system without using the Titan installer.

The installerless layout keeps the normal Titan boot architecture:

`Memory Card BOOT.ELF → Titan Bootloader → USB kernel.elf → Project Titan`

## BIG UPDATE

This release is called **BIG UPDATE** because it is not centered around one headline feature.

It represents another major consolidation of the entire Project Titan platform: networking, game patches, runtime behavior, stability, native applications, system services and many smaller improvements made throughout the project.

There is still work ahead — Project Titan remains an ambitious and actively developed system — but this revision moves the project considerably closer to the original goal:

**turning the PlayStation 2 into a modern, extensible system platform instead of simply giving it another game launcher.**

**Emotion enhanced.  
Feel the processing.**

